.TH PEKIT 1 2026-10-21 "Peios pekit 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
pekit \- build Peios packages from GCSL recipes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pekit init
.RI [ dir ]
.br
.B pekit package
.RB [ \-\-workspace
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-artifact\-dir
.IR dir ]
.I name
.br
.B pekit
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help | \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pekit
builds Peios packages from recipes written in GCSL and packs them with
.BR ppk (1).
.PP
A recipe workspace is a GCSL workspace: a directory tree whose root holds
.IR workspace.gcsl .
Its root also holds
.IR pekit\-include.gcsl ,
pekit's declarations of the definition types recipes use, which
.B pekit init
writes.
Every directory below the root sees them without importing them, and so
does a GCSL language server, which reads the file like any other.
.I workspace.gcsl
is an ordinary GCSL file that belongs to the workspace's author.
.PP
A recipe defines three kinds of definition:
.TP
.B source
An upstream source: a
.B url
and the
.B sha256
of what it serves.
.TP
.B build
The steps that make an install tree, laid out as
.IR /usr ,
from the unpacked source.
A
.B defmeta
gives the build's
.B source
and its
.BR dependencies .
.TP
.B package
A package: its
.BR build ,
the
.B files
it takes from the build's install tree, and its runtime
.BR dependencies .
.PP
A recipe file also gives
.BR "pekit = 1" ,
the recipe format it is written for, and the
.B version
and
.B revision
of its packages, which make the package's version:
.B version
.BR "= \(dq1.37.0\(dq" ,
.B revision
.B "= \(dq1\(dq"
makes 1.37.0\-1.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR init " [\fIdir\fR]"
Write
.I pekit\-include.gcsl
into the workspace at
.IR dir ,
the current directory by default, replacing any there, and an empty
.I workspace.gcsl
if there is none.
An existing
.I workspace.gcsl
is left as it is.
.TP
.BI package " name"
Build the package
.I name
and pack it into the artifact directory, printing its identity on standard
output.
If that version is already packed for the host's architecture,
.B pekit package
prints its identity and builds nothing.
.IP
Otherwise
.B pekit package
creates the artifact directory if it is missing and checks that it can
write there, then fetches the source of the package's build into its cache and checks its
SHA-256, unless the cache holds it already, then unpacks it into a work
directory and runs the build with the unpacked source as
.BR source_path ,
an empty directory as
.BR out_path ,
and the host's architecture as
.BR arch .
It then copies the files the package chooses from the install tree the
build returns and packs them as
.IR name @ version ,
for the host's architecture.
The work directory is removed afterwards.
.IP
Each entry of
.B files
maps a path in
.I /usr
to the path in the install tree it comes from.
Both are relative,
.BR / \-separated,
and have no
.B .\&
or
.B ..\&
segments.
A last segment of
.B *
on both sides takes every entry of a directory.
A directory is taken whole, and a symbolic link as it is, never followed.
.IP
The build runs on the host, with the host's tools, and only the
.B sh
calls of its steps reach outside GCSL.
Build and runtime dependencies are not supported yet: a recipe that gives
any is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-workspace " dir"
Read recipes from the workspace at
.IR dir ,
rather than the workspace the current directory is in.
.TP
.BI \-\-artifact\-dir " dir"
Store packages in
.IR dir ,
.I /system/artifacts
by default, as
.BR ppk (1)
does.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including printing help or the version.
.TP
.B 1
Failure, such as a workspace whose include file is not this pekit's, a
recipe with errors, an artifact directory pekit cannot write to, a source whose SHA-256 differs from the recipe's, a
build that fails, or a package version that is already packed with
different contents.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an unknown option or a missing argument.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
The base of pekit's cache,
.I ~/.cache
when it is unset or empty.
.TP
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
Set by
.B pekit package
for the build, replacing any value it is given, to the modification time
of the newest file in the unpacked source, so that tools that stamp a time
into what they make give the same result each time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME /peios/pekit/sources/sha256/ hash
A fetched source, named by its SHA-256.
.TP
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME /peios/pekit/work/
Work directories of builds in progress.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pekit init
Make the current directory a recipe workspace, or bring its
.I pekit\-include.gcsl
up to date.
.TP
.B pekit package net.busybox.busybox \-\-artifact\-dir artifacts
Build busybox from its recipe and pack it into
.IR artifacts .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ppk (1),
.BR gcsl (1)
